        "url": "https://x.com/exolabs/status/2092320487019880735",
        "text": "exo featured on Apple's new M5 Ultra Mac Studio and M6 / M5 Pro Mac Mini pages.\n\nOver the past year, we have worked closely with Apple on low-latency RDMA networking over Thunderbolt 5, enabling clusters of Macs to run massive models like Kimi K3 and GLM-5.3 at API speeds.\n\nWith RDMA, aggregate memory bandwidth across Macs scales ~linearly.\n\nA cluster of 4 x M5 Ultra Mac Studios scale to an aggregate memory bandwidth of ~4.8TB/s. Previously, these were speeds only achievable with data center GPUs.\n\nOur vision is a data center on every desk. Apple Silicon's superior memory unit economics, power efficiency, and out of the box experience for Local AI make that possible.\n\nThank you to @angeloskath, @awnihannun, @twid and countless others at Apple who tirelessly to bring this technology to the world.",
        "createdAt": "Tue Aug 25 18:37:32 +0000 2026",
        "retweetCount": 116,
        "replyCount": 62,
